Let $z:[t_0, +\infty [\rightarrow \mathcal{H}$ be a global solution trajectory of (DRYGRAD) where $f$ is assumed to be convex. Then, the following properties are satisfied

(i) $t\mapsto \| \dot{z} (t)\|$ is decreasing;
(ii) $\| \dot{z}(t)\| = o\left(\frac{1}{t}\right)$ as $t\to +\infty$.
